#
# Copy to .env and edit. Compose reads .env automatically; it is gitignored.
# Full descriptions of every variable live in the README's env tables.
#
# ONE THING TO GET RIGHT FIRST: the two key variables live on opposite sides
# of the container boundary, and they are easy to mix up.
#
#   TWIKI_KEY_PATH                     where the key is ON YOUR MACHINE.
#                                      Read only by compose.yml, to know what
#                                      to mount. No source file reads it.
#
#   TWIKI_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH  where the key is INSIDE the container.
#                                      The one the app actually reads
#                                      (src/github/auth.ts). compose.yml
#                                      pins it to /secrets/twiki.pem.
#
# So under compose you set the FIRST one and never the second. Setting the
# second here does nothing: compose declares it under `environment`, which
# beats `env_file`, and a host path would be meaningless inside the container
# anyway. What makes that costly is the failure it leads to - the mount then
# falls back to this file's default, Docker creates a MISSING mount source as
# an empty DIRECTORY rather than failing, and the app dies with EISDIR instead
# of saying the key is missing.
#
# Running the binary directly instead of through compose, it is the other way
# round: set TWIKI_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH to wherever the file is, and
# TWIKI_KEY_PATH does nothing. Same for the TRICORDER_ pair.

# Image to run. Defaults to the published one.
#
# To run what `make image` just built locally, set BOTH: that target tags
# $(IMAGE):$(TAG) with the Makefile's own defaults, which are `twiki:dev`.
# Changing only TAG here leaves IMAGE pointing at ghcr.io, and compose then
# fails trying to pull a tag that only exists on your machine.
#
#   IMAGE=twiki
#   TAG=dev
IMAGE=ghcr.io/no42-org/twiki
TAG=latest

# --- twiki (the write side) -------------------------------------------------
TWIKI_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# Host path. This file must exist before `make up`, and be readable by uid
# 65532, the image's non-root user.
TWIKI_KEY_PATH=./twiki.pem
# Start in shadow. Flip to enforce once you trust the digests.
TWIKI_MODE=shadow
TWIKI_POLL_MINUTES=60
TWIKI_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- gitricorder (the read side) --------------------------------------------
# A SEPARATE App from twiki's, read-only by construction (AD-21). Sharing one
# credential would give the dashboard the ability to write, which is the single
# thing its design rules out.
TRICORDER_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# Host path, same rules as twiki's above.
TRICORDER_KEY_PATH=./tricorder.pem
TRICORDER_TICK_SECONDS=60

# The dashboard is published on 127.0.0.1 only. There is no authentication in
# front of it; changing that binding exposes every collected alert.
TRICORDER_PORT=8787
